    "problem": "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I=\\{5,6,7\\},$ and\n${S}_{i}=[i,\\,i+1).$",
    "worked_solution": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{5}\\cup {S}_{6}\\cup {S}_{7} \\\\  & =[5,6)\\,\\cup \\,[6,7)\\,\\cup \\,[7,8) \\\\  & =[5,8).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
